{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This utility comes as a separate package and is available under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'@tanstack/query-async-storage-persister'"},{"type":"text","value":" import."}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"yarn add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"bun add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAsyncStoragePersister"},{"type":"text","value":" function"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a new asyncStoragePersister"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"you can pass any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"storage"},{"type":"text","value":" to it that adheres to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AsyncStorage"},{"type":"text","value":" interface - the example below uses the async-storage from React Native."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"storages that read and write synchronously, like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window.localstorage"},{"type":"text","value":", also adhere to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AsyncStorage"},{"type":"text","value":" interface and can therefore also be used with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAsyncStoragePersister"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrap your app by using "},{"type":"link","href":"./persistQueryClient.md#persistqueryclientprovider","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PersistQueryClientProvider"}]},{"type":"text","value":" component."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage'\nimport { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { PersistQueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query-persist-client'\nimport { createAsyncStoragePersister } from '@tanstack/query-async-storage-persister'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      gcTime: 1000 * 60 * 60 * 24, // 24 hours\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst asyncStoragePersister = createAsyncStoragePersister({\n  storage: AsyncStorage,\n})\n\nconst Root = () => (\n  <PersistQueryClientProvider\n    client={queryClient}\n    persistOptions={{ persister: asyncStoragePersister }}\n  >\n    <App />\n  </PersistQueryClientProvider>\n)\n\nexport default Root","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"retries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retries work the same as for a "},{"type":"link","href":"./createSyncStoragePersister.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SyncStoragePersister"}]},{"type":"text","value":", except that they can also be asynchronous. You can also use all the predefined retry handlers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createasyncstoragepersister","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAsyncStoragePersister"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call this function to create an asyncStoragePersister that you can use later with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistQueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"createAsyncStoragePersister(options: CreateAsyncStoragePersisterOptions)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface CreateAsyncStoragePersisterOptions {\n  /** The storage client used for setting an retrieving items from cache */\n  storage: AsyncStorage | undefined | null\n  /** The key to use when storing the cache to localStorage */\n  key?: string\n  /** To avoid localStorage spamming,\n   * pass a time in ms to throttle saving the cache to disk */\n  throttleTime?: number\n  /** How to serialize the data to storage */\n  serialize?: (client: PersistedClient) => MaybePromise<string>\n  /** How to deserialize the data from storage */\n  deserialize?: (cachedString: string) => MaybePromise<PersistedClient>\n  /** How to retry persistence on error **/\n  retry?: AsyncPersistRetryer\n}\n\ninterface AsyncStorage<TStorageValue = string> {\n  getItem: (key: string) => MaybePromise<TStorageValue | undefined | null>\n  setItem: (key: string, value: TStorageValue) => MaybePromise<unknown>\n  removeItem: (key: string) => MaybePromise<void>\n  entries?: () => MaybePromise<Array<[key: string, value: TStorageValue]>>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serialize"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deserialize"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks can return their results synchronously or asynchronously as promises."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default options are:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  key = `REACT_QUERY_OFFLINE_CACHE`,\n  throttleTime = 1000,\n  serialize = JSON.stringify,\n  deserialize = JSON.parse,\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"usage","text":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"retries","text":"Retries","level":2},{"id":"api","text":"API","level":2},{"id":"createasyncstoragepersister","text":"createAsyncStoragePersister","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Installation\n\nThis utility comes as a separate package and is available under the `'@tanstack/query-async-storage-persister'` import.\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nbun add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n- Import the `createAsyncStoragePersister` function\n- Create a new asyncStoragePersister\n  - you can pass any `storage` to it that adheres to the `AsyncStorage` interface - the example below uses the async-storage from React Native.\n  - storages that read and write synchronously, like `window.localstorage`, also adhere to the `AsyncStorage` interface and can therefore also be used with `createAsyncStoragePersister`.\n- Wrap your app by using [`PersistQueryClientProvider`](./persistQueryClient.md#persistqueryclientprovider) component.\n\n```tsx\nimport AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage'\nimport { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { PersistQueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query-persist-client'\nimport { createAsyncStoragePersister } from '@tanstack/query-async-storage-persister'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      gcTime: 1000 * 60 * 60 * 24, // 24 hours\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst asyncStoragePersister = createAsyncStoragePersister({\n  storage: AsyncStorage,\n})\n\nconst Root = () => (\n  <PersistQueryClientProvider\n    client={queryClient}\n    persistOptions={{ persister: asyncStoragePersister }}\n  >\n    <App />\n  </PersistQueryClientProvider>\n)\n\nexport default Root\n```\n\n## Retries\n\nRetries work the same as for a [SyncStoragePersister](./createSyncStoragePersister.md), except that they can also be asynchronous. You can also use all the predefined retry handlers.\n\n## API\n\n### `createAsyncStoragePersister`\n\nCall this function to create an asyncStoragePersister that you can use later with `persistQueryClient`.\n\n```tsx\ncreateAsyncStoragePersister(options: CreateAsyncStoragePersisterOptions)\n```\n\n### `Options`\n\n```tsx\ninterface CreateAsyncStoragePersisterOptions {\n  /** The storage client used for setting an retrieving items from cache */\n  storage: AsyncStorage | undefined | null\n  /** The key to use when storing the cache to localStorage */\n  key?: string\n  /** To avoid localStorage spamming,\n   * pass a time in ms to throttle saving the cache to disk */\n  throttleTime?: number\n  /** How to serialize the data to storage */\n  serialize?: (client: PersistedClient) => MaybePromise<string>\n  /** How to deserialize the data from storage */\n  deserialize?: (cachedString: string) => MaybePromise<PersistedClient>\n  /** How to retry persistence on error **/\n  retry?: AsyncPersistRetryer\n}\n\ninterface AsyncStorage<TStorageValue = string> {\n  getItem: (key: string) => MaybePromise<TStorageValue | undefined | null>\n  setItem: (key: string, value: TStorageValue) => MaybePromise<unknown>\n  removeItem: (key: string) => MaybePromise<void>\n  entries?: () => MaybePromise<Array<[key: string, value: TStorageValue]>>\n}\n```\n\nThe `serialize` and `deserialize` callbacks can return their results synchronously or asynchronously as promises.\n\nThe default options are:\n\n```tsx\n{\n  key = `REACT_QUERY_OFFLINE_CACHE`,\n  throttleTime = 1000,\n  serialize = JSON.stringify,\n  deserialize = JSON.parse,\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createAsyncStoragePersister\ntitle: createAsyncStoragePersister\n---\n\n## Installation\n\nThis utility comes as a separate package and is available under the `'@tanstack/query-async-storage-persister'` import.\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nbun add @tanstack/query-async-storage-persister @tanstack/react-query-persist-client\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n- Import the `createAsyncStoragePersister` function\n- Create a new asyncStoragePersister\n  - you can pass any `storage` to it that adheres to the `AsyncStorage` interface - the example below uses the async-storage from React Native.\n  - storages that read and write synchronously, like `window.localstorage`, also adhere to the `AsyncStorage` interface and can therefore also be used with `createAsyncStoragePersister`.\n- Wrap your app by using [`PersistQueryClientProvider`](./persistQueryClient.md#persistqueryclientprovider) component.\n\n```tsx\nimport AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage'\nimport { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { PersistQueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query-persist-client'\nimport { createAsyncStoragePersister } from '@tanstack/query-async-storage-persister'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient({\n  defaultOptions: {\n    queries: {\n      gcTime: 1000 * 60 * 60 * 24, // 24 hours\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nconst asyncStoragePersister = createAsyncStoragePersister({\n  storage: AsyncStorage,\n})\n\nconst Root = () => (\n  <PersistQueryClientProvider\n    client={queryClient}\n    persistOptions={{ persister: asyncStoragePersister }}\n  >\n    <App />\n  </PersistQueryClientProvider>\n)\n\nexport default Root\n```\n\n## Retries\n\nRetries work the same as for a [SyncStoragePersister](./createSyncStoragePersister.md), except that they can also be asynchronous. You can also use all the predefined retry handlers.\n\n## API\n\n### `createAsyncStoragePersister`\n\nCall this function to create an asyncStoragePersister that you can use later with `persistQueryClient`.\n\n```tsx\ncreateAsyncStoragePersister(options: CreateAsyncStoragePersisterOptions)\n```\n\n### `Options`\n\n```tsx\ninterface CreateAsyncStoragePersisterOptions {\n  /** The storage client used for setting an retrieving items from cache */\n  storage: AsyncStorage | undefined | null\n  /** The key to use when storing the cache to localStorage */\n  key?: string\n  /** To avoid localStorage spamming,\n   * pass a time in ms to throttle saving the cache to disk */\n  throttleTime?: number\n  /** How to serialize the data to storage */\n  serialize?: (client: PersistedClient) => MaybePromise<string>\n  /** How to deserialize the data from storage */\n  deserialize?: (cachedString: string) => MaybePromise<PersistedClient>\n  /** How to retry persistence on error **/\n  retry?: AsyncPersistRetryer\n}\n\ninterface AsyncStorage<TStorageValue = string> {\n  getItem: (key: string) => MaybePromise<TStorageValue | undefined | null>\n  setItem: (key: string, value: TStorageValue) => MaybePromise<unknown>\n  removeItem: (key: string) => MaybePromise<void>\n  entries?: () => MaybePromise<Array<[key: string, value: TStorageValue]>>\n}\n```\n\nThe `serialize` and `deserialize` callbacks can return their results synchronously or asynchronously as promises.\n\nThe default options are:\n\n```tsx\n{\n  key = `REACT_QUERY_OFFLINE_CACHE`,\n  throttleTime = 1000,\n  serialize = JSON.stringify,\n  deserialize = JSON.parse,\n}\n```\n"}
